 now consumable items that  restore those charges so you know what  all this means it means we can finally  play sorcerers properly in dark side  to number three so do you remember  getting killed on your first playthrough  by some guy who finished the game and  cut all the good equipment just so he  could kill you with it  so do I those were good times but now  some of the stronger armors actually  have stat requirements now this is a  great change since it will do a lot to  reduced winking you'll remember in Dark  Souls that people would be so level one  with decent armor sets and while armor  doesn't make a huge difference in the  grand scheme of things I think at least  it indicates that from software have  ganking in mind when they work on game  balance number four is a really cool  change  there were always lots of stories of  people who put their controller down and  then press the bumpers accidentally and  hidden NBC in front of them killing them  or a growing them but in Dark Souls 2  when you kill an NBC a gravestone will  appear in their place you can then  revive the NPC temporarily for a fairly  extreme price allowing you to browse  their wares and talk to them again so  this is a bit more forgiving but it  still punishes you for doing something  stupid I just wonder do you think they  know that they're dead because I  probably wouldn't want to sell my items  to the person who just killed me anyway  number 5 you can now get damaged or  poised broken during any animation  you're no longer invincible when  performing a riposte backstabbing  pulling a lever opening a door or going  through a fog gate  on the same note you can also cancel the  animation by pressing the button again  which I remember my friend tried to go  through the fog gate to fight the mirror  night and he just kept spamming the X  button to go through the fog gate and  essentially what it was doing was  pressing X and then cancelling it and  going through and cancelling and going  through until the enemies just came up  behind him and completely destroyed him  but yeah so in Dark Souls 2 this is  going to be a thing  it means backstabs are going to be less  of an option when fighting enemies in  groups and also running past can be  difficult now since developers could  just bottleneck you by putting a door in  your way meaning you could get attacked  while you open that door we're in Dark  Souls you're invincible when you open  that door and that's it overall these  are some really cool changes let me know  what you think they make me really  excited for the game  let me know how many you got out of five  as well and feel free to subscribe if  you want to be prepared for the next  episode in this series cheers guys  I'll catch you next time Dark Souls 2 is  shaping up to be a much more difficult  game than its predecessor  welcome again guys to Souls news an  embargo has just lifted on some more  details about Dark Souls 2 and these  these are probably the best facts we've  heard for a while so sit back relax and  let me share them with you if you want  to skip ahead to something more  interesting  check the description the three biggest  pieces of news are as follows one summon  phantoms now have a temporary lifespan -  every time you died
 

